# NeuroNote environment variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your own values.
# Never commit .env.local to Git — it is already covered by .gitignore.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NeuroNote currently reads NO build-time environment variables.
#
# Every credential is entered in the app's SYSTEM tab and stored in your
# browser's localStorage on your own device:
#
#   - OpenAI API key
#   - AssemblyAI API key
#   - Google OAuth Client ID   (optional, for Calendar + Tasks)
#   - Microsoft Azure Client ID and Tenant ID (optional, for Outlook + To Do)
#
# That is deliberate: keys never enter the bundle, never reach a server, and
# never end up in a deployment's environment. This file exists so the project
# has the usual place to put a variable if one is ever added.
#
# `vercel link` / `vercel env pull` will also write a VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN into
# .env.local. That is a Vercel CLI credential, not an app setting — leave it
# out of version control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
